A||N||6||jeffreyeffrey||My Fiero Won't Fire||||8||
Z||000000||jeffreyeffrey||05-17-2001||01:00 PM||||no more than 24 hours back from the shop where I had new intake manifold gaskets, and valve cover gaskets put on, I took my '86 GT to town to get fuel. I got home and parked it, that night when I tried to start it all the car would do was turn over and turn over, it won't even make a pop. It's been like that for a week now. You can smell unburned fuel so it's not fuel pump, and there's spark, (at least on the 3 plugs I can get to) so I'm baffled, any ideas on what could have failed to make it not start after running fine an hour beforehand? Thanks||||reg||8
Z||000001||fyerstarter||05-17-2001||01:10 PM||||Is there a potato stuck in your exhaust pipe?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>...or perhaps more realistically a clogged cat.<P><BR>Hrrrmmm... some people may consider the fact that there fiero wont "fire" a good thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||fyerstarter||05-17-2001||01:12 PM||||OK a few more practical suggestions:<P>-Check the plugs to see if they are wet with fuel<BR>-Check the fuel pressure at the schrader valve near the right side of your intake manifold<P>Good luck. My Fiero won't fire right now either  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||05-17-2001||01:32 PM|||| For what it,s worth.<BR>Last Saturday I came home late in my 84 SE, It was running fine. Next morning it would not fire. I thought it might be moisture since there was a heavy dew. tried several things with no luck. Swapped control modules with a running car. It fired right up. Wierd that the module died during the night.||||reg||1
Z||000004||loafer87gt||05-17-2001||04:54 PM||||My Toyota truck was doing the same thing and it turned out that the contacts on the starter needed to be cleaned. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tweek||05-18-2001||12:22 AM||||My 84 was doing this earlier today and was really pi$$ing me off...  all I did was remove the wire that goes from the distributer to the coil, and put it back on, musta been loose cause she fired right up.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DavidHenshaw||05-18-2001||01:42 PM||||JefferyEffery, is that your real name, you are almost for sure suffering from ignition control module non workus. Your car turns over but will not start and sounds as if its getting no gas. If its not the ICM it may be a bad pick up coil inside the distributor which will look rusty if its bad. <P>Take the ICM to a local auto parts store and they can check it for you.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
